  "diary": "The air in Lodhi Gardens was clear, but the heat in my hand was not. I bought a chai from Sunil for twenty rupees, a small cost for the privilege of arguing with a register while the steam rose. The file on my desk holds a dead professor as a living Joint Secretary. This is not a slip of ink; it is a contradiction in the Notion. The state’s sign-system has made the error an institutional fact. I walked three kilometres, not to solve it, but to let the distinction between sign and Notion cool in the body. At home, Ramesh’s practical questions settled the household: the estate office is shut on Sundays, and the dhobi, Salim of Tughlakabad, comes on Thursday for two hundred rupees. My ledger said Saturday and three hundred. The state’s money cannot be settled by memory. I traced the error to its source, not to smooth it over with household convenience. I sat with the vouchers, ensuring the public imprest remains separate from my own cash. At dinner, I insisted Ramesh sit. A servant’s standing is the house’s order, but I will not eat alone in a house where my man stands. The contradiction remains on the desk, a guest who will not leave. It must wait until Monday at ten. The owl spreads its wings only with the dusk; the notion must rest before it can be thought again.",
